Subject: Preserve web seed file availability after transient HTTP errors
Base: libtorrent v2.0.15
Base-Commit: 1eb18faeae156d8dbbab42935c082f8b81f50989
Base-Blob: src/web_peer_connection.cpp 9c5d6eb990c5cbe694bd66b730a630f24da763c4

A non-success HTTP response currently clears availability of the requested
file. For a single-file URL seed this prevents later connections, despite
handle_error() scheduling a retry. Preserve availability only for HTTP
408, 429, 500, 502, 503 and 504 so the existing retry path can reconnect.

This local dependency patch applies to the pinned libtorrent source used by
qBittorrent 5.2.4 on Windows, Linux and Docker. It retains existing handling
of other HTTP errors, hash failures, bans, authentication and redirects.
Retry-After and urlseed_wait_retry retain their existing native behavior;
no torrent restart, URL reset or additional network request is introduced.

Runtime regression: own loopback URL seed first returns 503, then valid 206;
the patched client must complete with a matching SHA-256 without user action.
The stock loopback transfer with valid 206 completes; injected 503 stalls.

diff --git a/src/web_peer_connection.cpp b/src/web_peer_connection.cpp
--- a/src/web_peer_connection.cpp
+++ b/src/web_peer_connection.cpp
@@ -535,6 +535,22 @@
 
 namespace {
 
+	bool isTransientHttpError(int const status)
+	{
+		switch (status)
+		{
+		case 408:
+		case 429:
+		case 500:
+		case 502:
+		case 503:
+		case 504:
+			return true;
+		default:
+			return false;
+		}
+	}
+
 	std::string get_peer_name(http_parser const& p, std::string const& host)
 	{
 		std::string const& server_version = p.header("server");
@@ -904,7 +920,10 @@
 			// if the status code is not one of the accepted ones, abort
 			if (!is_ok_status(m_parser.status_code()))
 			{
-				if (!m_file_requests.empty())
+				// A transient response does not imply that the file is missing.
+				// Keep it available for the retry scheduled by handle_error().
+				if (!m_file_requests.empty()
+					&& !isTransientHttpError(m_parser.status_code()))
 				{
 					file_request_t const& file_req = m_file_requests.front();
 					m_web->have_files.resize(t->torrent_file().num_files(), true);
